source: tests/cli_golden.rs
expression: help
---
List installed plugins and their active versions

Usage: aura plugins list [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --mode <MODE>
          Session mode for the desktop window or terminal. Overrides the daemon default (`AURA_DEFAULT_MODE`); the kernel denies any tool call the mode does not allow

          Possible values:
          - agent: Full unrestricted operation subject to user permissions
          - plan:  Read + markdown writes + read-only subprocesses
          - ask:   Read-only (the terminal's `read-only` mode)
          - debug: Read + sandboxed probes only

      --approval <APPROVAL>
          What tool calls ask first: `yolo` runs everything with commands confined to writing inside the working folder, `ask` asks for anything not on the allow list, `strict` asks for everything but reads. Overrides `AURA_TUI_APPROVAL`; `-p` defaults to `yolo` in agent mode

          Possible values:
          - yolo:   Run everything; commands can write only inside the working folder
          - ask:    Ask for anything not on the project's allow list
          - strict: Ask for everything except reads, even what the allow list covers

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
